# Database files
*.db
data/
# Recovery copies of data/, kept beside it. Gigabytes of SQLite and FAISS, and
# the only route back to a previous population — worth guarding from an
# absent-minded `git add -A` as much as from deletion.
#
# Each one holds the same filenames as data/, so going back to it is: stop the
# stack, then either copy its contents over data/, or leave it where it is and
# point DB_FILE and the HUMAN_/MOUSE_ index and mapping paths in .env at it.
# Take the .db, its -wal and -shm sidecars, and each index with its .meta.json
# together — an index whose sidecar names a different model is refused at load,
# and a .db separated from its -wal is missing whatever had not been checkpointed.
data_backup_*/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

